# Ordinary source is normalised to LF in the repository.
# (The last matching pattern wins, so this general rule comes first.)
*                    text=auto eol=lf

# The authored templates, their catalogues and the assets the site serves are
# byte-exact inputs: the whole point of this project is that what ships is what
# was authored, down to the byte. Line-ending conversion would rewrite every
# one of them on checkout — LF on Linux, CRLF on Windows — and the rendered
# pages would then differ from the originals depending on where they were built.
#
# `-text` disables conversion entirely for these paths.
content-source/**    -text
apps/web/public/**   -text
tools/fidelity.hashes.json -text

# Binary, in case the wildcard above is ever loosened.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
